                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.515/815: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-04T12:00:00+08:00">November 4,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 4—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference my strictly confidential November 2, 11 p.m., I am informed the British
                    authorities have issued an Order in Council advising British nationals to comply
                    with the decree of the Chinese Government regarding the nationalization of
                    silver.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
